WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.516 --> 00:00:14.660
leaving the station, Phileas Fogg quietly returned to his house on Savile Row.

2
00:00:15.981 --> 00:00:18.603
His neighbors would have been surprised to learn that he had returned.

3
00:00:19.924 --> 00:00:22.066
The doors and windows of his house remained closed.

4
00:00:22.867 --> 00:00:23.847
The building was quiet.

5
00:00:27.951 --> 00:00:29.052
Mr. Fogg was ruined!

6
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.361
And by the blundering of a detective!

7
00:00:33.362 --> 00:00:36.644
Only a few pounds were left in the carpetbag that had traveled the world with him.

8
00:00:37.665 --> 00:00:43.169
All that remained of his fortune–twenty-thousand pounds deposited at the bank–he now owed to his friends at the

9
00:00:43.189 --> 00:00:43.850
Reform Club.

10
00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:49.233
He set aside a room in the house for Aouda, who was overwhelmed with grief at her protector's

11
00:00:49.273 --> 00:00:53.817
misfortune. Passepartout was also desperately concerned for his master.

12
00:00:54.677 --> 00:00:56.178
He watched all evening as Mr.

13
00:00:56.238 --> 00:00:58.060
Fogg sat silently in his armchair.

14
00:00:59.112 --> 00:01:00.173
Late at night Mr.

15
00:01:00.213 --> 00:01:01.795
Fogg climbed the stairs to bed.

16
00:01:03.176 --> 00:01:06.559
Many a ruined man has chosen suicide, and fearful that Mr.

17
00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:11.183
Fogg planned some desperate act, Passepartout waited faithfully all night at his master's door.

18
00:01:12.604 --> 00:01:13.385
In the morning Mr.

19
00:01:13.405 --> 00:01:17.949
Fogg called Passepartout into his room and asked him to look after Aouda's breakfast and lunch.

20
00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:21.212
Mr. Fogg would be too busy setting his affairs in order.

21
00:01:22.112 --> 00:01:25.936
In the evening he would ask permission to have a few moments of conversation with the lady.

22
00:01:26.996 --> 00:01:30.998
Passepartout felt so horrible and responsible that he could contain himself no longer.

23
00:01:31.018 --> 00:01:32.658
"My master!

24
00:01:32.719 --> 00:01:33.339
Mr. Fogg!"

25
00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:34.139
he cried.

26
00:01:34.159 --> 00:01:35.680
"Don't you blame me?

27
00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:40.062
It was my fault that—" "I blame no one," returned Mr.

28
00:01:40.082 --> 00:01:41.242
Fogg. "Go!"

29
00:01:42.983 --> 00:01:44.263
Passepartout left Mr.

30
00:01:44.303 --> 00:01:47.305
Fogg's room and went to deliver the master's message to Aouda.

31
00:01:48.505 --> 00:01:51.366
Mr. Fogg shut himself in his room and busied himself at his desk.

32
00:01:52.827 --> 00:01:54.728
Passepartout also had a matter to settle.

33
00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:58.703
In the mailbox that morning, he had found a bill from the gas company.

34
00:01:59.583 --> 00:02:03.026
He remembered at once that the heater in his room had been burning for eighty days!

35
00:02:03.947 --> 00:02:06.990
He wasted not one minute more and rushed to his room to shut it off.

36
00:02:09.812 --> 00:02:11.593
At half-past seven that evening, Mr.

37
00:02:11.613 --> 00:02:12.954
Fogg knocked on Aouda's door.

38
00:02:14.336 --> 00:02:16.097
No emotion was visible on his face.

39
00:02:17.038 --> 00:02:19.400
He entered and sat several minutes without speaking.

40
00:02:20.241 --> 00:02:24.064
Then he said, "Madam, please forgive me for bringing you to England.

41
00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:28.522
When I decided to bring you so far away from your country, I was rich.

42
00:02:30.023 --> 00:02:32.825
I was going to put a portion of my fortune at your disposal.

43
00:02:33.605 --> 00:02:35.266
Then you would have been free and happy.

44
00:02:35.847 --> 00:02:37.207
But now I am ruined."

45
00:02:37.227 --> 00:02:38.928
"I know it, Mr.

46
00:02:38.968 --> 00:02:40.129
Fogg," said Aouda.

47
00:02:40.149 --> 00:02:43.971
"And I ask in return, will you forgive me for following you?

48
00:02:44.912 --> 00:02:47.533
For, perhaps, delaying you and contributing to your loss."

49
00:02:47.553 --> 00:02:51.676
"Madam, you could not have remained in India.

50
00:02:52.428 --> 00:02:56.770
Your safety depended on traveling as far as possible from those chasing you."

51
00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:58.671
"But what will become of you?"

52
00:02:59.131 --> 00:02:59.731
asked Aouda.

53
00:02:59.751 --> 00:03:02.572
"I have need of nothing," said Fogg.

54
00:03:02.592 --> 00:03:06.754
"Surely poverty will not overtake a man like you," said Aouda.

55
00:03:06.774 --> 00:03:12.177
"Your friends—" "They are not close friends," he replied simply.

56
00:03:12.197 --> 00:03:17.579
"Your relatives—" "I no longer have any relatives."

57
00:03:17.619 --> 00:03:19.520
"Mr. Fogg," said Aouda, rising.

58
00:03:20.276 --> 00:03:22.457
"May I offer you a kinswoman and a friend?

59
00:03:23.137 --> 00:03:24.577
Will you have me for your wife?"

60
00:03:26.458 --> 00:03:27.338
At this, Mr.

61
00:03:27.358 --> 00:03:28.578
Fogg rose in his turn.

62
00:03:29.298 --> 00:03:32.039
There was a light in his eyes and a slight trembling of his lips.

63
00:03:32.759 --> 00:03:34.080
Aouda looked into his face.

64
00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:38.801
Fogg shut his eyes for an instant as if to avoid her look, but when he opened them

65
00:03:38.861 --> 00:03:40.341
again, he said, "I love you.

66
00:03:41.062 --> 00:03:45.363
Yes, by all that is holiest, I love you, and I am entirely yours."

67
00:03:45.383 --> 00:03:49.384
"Ah!" cried Aouda, pressing his hand to her heart.

68
00:03:50.976 --> 00:03:53.297
Passepartout was summoned and appeared immediately.

69
00:03:54.017 --> 00:03:59.239
Mr. Fogg still held Aouda's hand in his own, and Passepartout immediately understood what had happened.

70
00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.701
Passepartout's face became as radiant as the tropical sun at its highest.

71
00:04:04.481 --> 00:04:09.243
Mr. Fogg asked him if it was not too late to notify the Reverend Samuel Wilson that very

72
00:04:09.343 --> 00:04:15.026
evening. Passepartout smiled one of his warmest smiles and said, "It is never too late!"

73
00:04:16.066 --> 00:04:18.107
It was five minutes past eight in the evening.

74
00:04:18.127 --> 00:04:20.528
"Will the wedding be tomorrow?"

75
00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:21.881
asked Passepartout.

76
00:04:21.901 --> 00:04:23.901
"Tomorrow," said Mr.

77
00:04:23.941 --> 00:04:25.302
Fogg, turning to Aouda.

78
00:04:25.322 --> 00:04:29.244
"Monday." "Yes, Monday," she replied.

79
00:04:30.084 --> 00:04:33.145
Passepartout hurried off as fast as his legs could carry him.

80
00:04:39.908 --> 00:04:41.508
At least something good came out of our trip.

81
00:04:42.109 --> 00:04:44.730
Mr. Fogg and Aouda are in love and will get married!

82
00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:48.171
I must find Reverend Wilson and start preparing for the wedding.

83
00:04:48.891 --> 00:04:49.792
There is so much to do!

84
00:04:50.572 --> 00:04:52.754
Did you know that most brides in England wear white?

85
00:04:53.374 --> 00:04:58.097
This tradition was started when Queen Victoria got married in 1840 and wore a white dress.

86
00:04:59.318 --> 00:05:03.181
Before that brides wore just about any color, with red being quite a popular choice.

87
00:05:04.121 --> 00:05:04.642
As for Mr.

88
00:05:04.682 --> 00:05:06.743
Fogg, well, he won't be wearing white!

89
00:05:07.404 --> 00:05:11.246
He might wear a frock coat, the long dress coat that is traditional for Victorian gentlemen.

90
00:05:12.307 --> 00:05:15.029
But today many men are wearing morning coats to weddings.

91
00:05:15.749 --> 00:05:19.152
A morning coat is cut short in the front with two long tails in the back.

92
00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:21.361
A morning coat is black or gray.

93
00:05:22.381 --> 00:05:25.162
After the church wedding, it is customary to have a wedding breakfast.

94
00:05:26.322 --> 00:05:28.503
I must be sure to reserve a special corner in Mr.

95
00:05:28.543 --> 00:05:32.605
Fogg's house where Aouda can receive the guests who come to congratulate the happy couple.

96
00:05:33.465 --> 00:05:34.925
After the reception, perhaps Mr.

97
00:05:34.945 --> 00:05:36.646
Fogg and Aouda will go on a honeymoon.

98
00:05:37.206 --> 00:05:39.347
Please forgive me, readers, if I do not linger much longer.

99
00:05:39.807 --> 00:05:41.428
Why, I have a wedding to plan!
